# Draft: combase: Implement remaining restricted WinRT error handling APIs.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11993 state=opened
# Wine-Bug: https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=58900

Depends on !9332 and !10659.

This is a follow-up to the restricted WinRT error handling work in !9332 and !10659.

The implementation was reworked to use the restricted error infrastructure introduced by !9332 instead of maintaining a separate restricted error object implementation.

This series adds implementations and tests for:

- RoClearError()
- RoGetMatchingRestrictedErrorInfo()
- RoCaptureErrorContext()
- RoTransformError()
- RoTransformErrorW()

It also improves the existing RoReportUnhandledError() semi-stub by handling the supplied IRestrictedErrorInfo object.

RoClearError clears the current thread error object without creating COM TLS state when none exists.

RoGetMatchingRestrictedErrorInfo returns the current restricted error information when its HRESULT matches the requested value, and otherwise originates matching restricted error information.

RoCaptureErrorContext captures a stack backtrace and stores it in Wine's restricted error object for later error-context handling.

RoTransformError() and RoTransformErrorW() implement HRESULT transformation, message handling, error reporting flag handling, restricted error creation, and preservation of captured error context.

RoReportUnhandledError validates and handles the supplied restricted error information. Windows Global Error Handler / WER integration is still not implemented.

Conformance tests are added for the new functionality under dlls/combase/tests.

The combase tests pass locally in a 32-bit Wine prefix.

The first eight commits in this MR belong to the prerequisite !9332 and !10659 series. Once those merge, this branch can be rebased onto current master so that only the follow-up commits remain.
